.TH CTI-PODPROBE 1 "2026-11-03" "cti-agent" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-podprobe \- read one window of the Proofpoint on Demand Log API and print aggregate counts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti\-podprobe
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR TIME ]
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR TIME ]
.RB [ \-\-type
.IR TYPE ]
.RB [ \-\-top
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-bytes
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.RB [ \-\-idle
.IR DURATION ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-podprobe
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-podprobe
is a read-only probe, run by hand. It opens one archive read of the
Proofpoint on Demand (PoD) Log API, counts what the stream contains, and
prints the counts: events per direction, route names, DMARC and SPF results,
the header-From domains and DKIM data of outbound mail, and inbound mail that
uses this organisation's domains.
It exists to show what the stream holds for this tenant before the domains
lane depends on it; the lane itself is not built.
.PP
It prints counts only. It never prints or stores a message, an address, a
subject or the token, and it sends nothing. Distinct keys per table are
capped, and key text is shortened and sanitised, so a hostile stream cannot
grow it without bound.
.PP
The service allows one session per token. A second connection with the same
token is refused with HTTP 409, so do not run the probe while another client
uses the token.
.SH OPTIONS
Go's flag syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash
.RB ( \-json ),
and a value may follow
.B =
or a space.
.TP
.BI \-\-since " TIME"
Start of the window, such as
.BR 2026\-11\-02T10:00:00\-0500 .
RFC 3339 is also accepted. The window must start more than an hour ago:
archive reads only.
Default: the hour that began 3 hours ago.
.TP
.BI \-\-to " TIME"
End of the window, same format. Must be after
.BR \-\-since .
Default: one hour after
.BR \-\-since .
.TP
.BI \-\-type " TYPE"
Stream type:
.BR message ,
.B maillog
or
.BR audit .
Default:\~\fBmessage\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
Rows to print per table.
Default:\~\fB20\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the aggregate as one indented JSON object instead of text.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-bytes " N"
Stop after reading this many bytes of messages. The counts then cover only
part of the window, and a note says so.
Default:\~\fB209715200\fR (200 MB).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Give up after this long.
Default:\~\fB10m\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-idle " DURATION"
Treat the window as finished when no data arrives for this long.
Default:\~\fB1m30s\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Read from the environment or
.IR fleet.env .
There is deliberately no flag for the token: a flag lands in shell history and
the process list.
.TP
.B POD_CLUSTER_ID
The PoD cluster ID, shown at the top right of the management interface.
Required.
.TP
.B POD_API_TOKEN
A Log API token created for the fleet alone (Email Protection portal,
Settings, API Key Management). Required.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/fleet.env
Holds both settings; 0640 root:ctiagent. The probe writes no file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The counts were printed, including when the read stopped at
.B \-\-max\-bytes
or went idle.
.TP
.B 1
A setting is missing, a time is invalid or too recent, or the service refused
or broke the read (a 409 means the token is in use elsewhere).
Go's flag package also uses 1 here for an unknown option.
.SH EXAMPLES
One archived hour:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-podprobe \e
  \-\-since 2026\-11\-02T10:00:00\-0500 \-\-to 2026\-11\-02T11:00:00\-0500
.EE
.PP
The default hour, as JSON, with a smaller cap:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-podprobe \-\-json \-\-max\-bytes 5242880
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-domains (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md, section 11g part 7, "The PoD Log API".
